%% ======================================================================================
%% K0-K1 BRIDGE - DETAILED ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM (v2 — aligned with bridge_system_design.md)
%% ======================================================================================
%% Created:  2026-02-01 (v1, original)
%% Rewrite:  2026-05-05 (v2, this file)
%% v2 amendments vs v1 (see docs/architecture/whiteboard_k1/bridge_system_design.md):
%%   - Deployment: v1 ships cloud-K0 multi-tenant; K1-only on devices.
%%     K0-on-every-device collapsed to a single "v2: home K0 (deferred)" annotation.
%%   - Sync: explicit L1 family-memory / L2 family-tool-state / L3 SessionState model
%%     replaces the undifferentiated FamilySyncAdapter+P07 wiring.
%%   - Multi-tenancy: cloud K0 internally partitioned by (tenant_id, user_id).
%%   - MS-2.5 substrate added: contract registry (bridge/contracts/_meta + manifests),
%%     codegen (tooling/contracts), CI gates (tooling/ci), CA bundle for manifest signing.
%%   - Crypto reality: Ed25519 via bridge/core/signing.py + per-device verify keys via
%%     ProvisioningLedger.DeviceKey. Removed v1's invented HMAC RequestSigner +
%%     CapabilityToken/TokenIssuer (explicit v1 non-goals).
%%   - Deleted v1 non-goals: FlatBufferCodec (JSON only), gRPCAdapter (HTTP only),
%%     P2PManager/STUN/TURN/WebRTC (deferred post-v2), marketplace UI / external CA.
%%   - IBridgePort: three real surfaces shown with MS-2.5 PR#1 rename targets
%%     (IBridgeRuntime, IFabricK0Port, IPlannerWritePort) instead of one abstract port.
%%   - Outbox enriched: dead_letter table, per-contract max_queue_age, drain_rate_per_sec.
%%   - DEGRADED-mode auto-derived from manifest fields, not a hand-coded matrix.
%%   - Wall-violation annotations on the two known production import violations.
%% Remaining v2 risks/conflicts the diagram surfaces:
%%   - bridge/_generated/ tree must stay K0/K1-disjoint (wall holds inside generated code)
%%   - manifest signing CA (familyos_root_v1) is a SEPARATE trust root from envelope
%%     signing (per-device keys via ProvisioningLedger). The two are explicitly distinct.
%% ======================================================================================

